Hi Jessie,

The ploidy.mean.cn <http://ploidy.mean.cn> is the weighted mean of the segments copy number.
In theory, this and the ploidy.estimate should be very close, but as you can see, it's not always the case.

Looking at your results, there is a wide confidence interval around the ploidy estimate, if this is WES there might be biases effecting the depth ratio profile, there are many factors that could result in such difference.
As a rule of thumb, when there are discrepancies in the two values, the ploidy.mean.cn <http://ploidy.mean.cn> is more correct, since it represent the segments and not an estimate of the model.

Best

Francesco

